---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import '../../styles/image-bench.css';
---
<Layout title="Color Workshop" description="Refine a palette, make a gradient, and check text contrast. Local color tools for a work of your own.">
<section class="bench wrap" id="color-workshop"><header class="bench-heading"><div><a class="bench-back" href="/tools/">← BACK TO THE TOOLBOX</a><h1>Color <em>Workshop.</em></h1><p>Find a color. Give it a role. Take the CSS.</p></div><a href="/tools/image/" class="bench-back">EXTRACT FROM AN IMAGE ↗</a></header><p id="color-status" class="bench-status" role="status" aria-live="polite">Everything stays in this tab unless you export it.</p>
<div class="color-workshop">
  <section><div class="bench-section-title"><h2>Two colors, one gradient</h2><span>FORMAT / BLEND</span></div><div class="color-pair"><label>First color <input id="color-a" value="#ad99e5" spellcheck="false"/></label><label>Second color <input id="color-b" value="#c6eaa5" spellcheck="false"/></label></div><div class="color-pair"><label>Pick first color <input id="color-picker" type="color" value="#ad99e5"/></label><label>Gradient angle <input id="color-angle" type="range" min="0" max="360" value="135"/><output id="color-angle-value">135°</output></label></div><div class="color-gradient" id="color-gradient"></div><div class="bench-toolbar">{['hex','rgb','hsl','css'].map(format=><button data-color-copy={format}>Copy {format.toUpperCase()}</button>)}<button id="color-reset">Reset gradient</button></div><pre id="color-output" tabindex="0" aria-label="Color formats and gradient CSS"></pre></section>
  <section><div class="bench-section-title"><h2>Words that can be read</h2><span>TEXT CONTRAST</span></div><div class="color-pair"><label>Foreground <input id="color-foreground" value="#25322d"/></label><label>Background <input id="color-background" value="#f5f0e4"/></label></div><button id="color-swap">Swap foreground / background</button><div id="color-sample" class="color-card"><strong>A clear thought.</strong><p>Some words need room. Every word needs enough contrast.</p></div><p id="color-ratio" class="bench-help"></p><table class="color-table"><thead><tr><th>WCAG AA text</th><th>Required</th><th>Result</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Normal text</td><td>4.5:1</td><td id="color-normal"></td></tr><tr><td>Large text</td><td>3:1</td><td id="color-large"></td></tr></tbody></table><p class="bench-help">Opaque sRGB colors only. Large text means at least 18 pt (24 px), or 14 pt (about 18.7 px) bold. This checks one text/color pair, not the accessibility of an entire page. <a href="https://www.w3.org/WAI/WCAG22/Understanding/contrast-minimum.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">W3C guidance ↗</a></p></section>
  <section class="color-palette"><div class="bench-section-title"><h2>A palette of your own</h2><span>1–8 COLORS / EXPLICIT ASSIGNMENT</span></div><p class="bench-help">Incoming colors never replace the gradient or contrast pair automatically. Choose a role below each swatch.</p><label>Palette name <input id="color-palette-name" maxlength="80" value="First palette"/></label><div id="color-list" class="color-editor-list"></div><div class="bench-toolbar"><button id="color-add" class="bench-primary">Add color</button><button id="color-copy-all">Copy all HEX</button><button id="color-copy-variables">Copy CSS variables</button><button id="color-download-css">Download CSS</button><button id="color-export">Export palette JSON</button><button id="color-import">Import palette JSON</button><input id="color-file" type="file" accept=".json" hidden/></div><pre id="color-palette-output" tabindex="0" aria-label="Palette CSS"></pre><p class="bench-help">No automatic palette storage. Download a JSON backup before leaving. Imported palettes are limited to 16 KB.</p></section>
</div></section><script>import '../../scripts/color-workshop';</script>
</Layout>
